  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote the fireworks scene in `src/main.ts`, but I could not run it or check it against the real Aura3D types. `@aura3d/engine` is not installed in this sandbox (`node_modules/@aura3d` is empty). The only typecheck error is \"Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'\". Calls I wasn't sure of are `setInstances` on runtime nodes, the sphere `params` names (`widthSegments`/`heightSegments`) and `opacity` on emissive materials. They are based on the docs and `llms.txt` and have not been compiled or rendered.\n\nWhat the code does:\n- **Scene:** a dark gradient sky with about 520 emissive star spheres, a glossy translucent water plane, and a dark shoreline with buildings, hills, a pier, a lamp and boats. Some building windows glow. The camera is fixed and bloom is on.\n- **Sparks:** emissive instanced spheres, one pool per colour (gold, red, blue, green, violet). Each pool has a mirrored copy under the water, shrunk and rippled, so the burst reflections show through the translucent water.\n- **Rockets:** they launch from the shoreline at irregular intervals, sometimes two at once. Each has a glowing head, a trail and falling embers. On reaching apex it bursts into a spherical shell of 85 to 130 sparks that fade under gravity and drag in about 1.6 to 2.9 seconds. Colours cycle through a shuffled bag. About 45% of bursts are \"streak\" bursts, where every spark drags a 4-ghost trail.\n- **Lighting:** a pool of 4 coloured point lights (placed at the burst and fading over 2 seconds) and the hemisphere light both react to bursts. They tint the water and shoreline. Each burst also spawns a faint translucent glow sphere to brighten the sky.\n- **State:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` (`bursts` and `activeParticles`) is updated every frame. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after the app is ready.\n\nI haven't seen a frame. Light intensities, bloom strength and sky brightness are estimates and may need tuning once it renders.",
